and have them all memorized and use

00:10:18.612 --> 00:10:21.233
that to give myself an edge.

00:10:21.233 --> 00:10:24.785
Even when I was in college,
I'd be in the library reading

00:10:24.785 --> 00:10:27.906
business books and just looking
for business biographies

00:10:27.906 --> 00:10:31.199
and just reading all I
could about business.

00:10:31.199 --> 00:10:33.926
When I had MicroSolutions and, you know,

00:10:33.926 --> 00:10:35.583
I started with no money.

00:10:35.583 --> 00:10:39.744
I would pull all nighters in
front of borrowed computers,

00:10:39.744 --> 00:10:43.198
teaching myself software
and how to program.

00:10:43.198 --> 00:10:45.571
- Life demands that you pick up the pace.

00:10:45.571 --> 00:10:49.110
If you don't pick up the pace,
you're gon' be left behind.

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:51.224
I'm amazed at the people that

00:10:51.224 --> 00:10:54.825
lack the flexibility to pick up the pace.

00:10:54.825 --> 00:10:56.081
They just get in a rut.

00:10:56.081 --> 00:11:00.816
"I'll stroll down here,
and I'm gon' stroll back."

00:11:00.816 --> 00:11:04.249
"I'm gon' stroll over here,
I'm gon' stroll over there."

00:11:04.249 --> 00:11:07.279
One of the most amazing
things about the disaster

00:11:07.279 --> 00:11:09.626
at Malaysia is that, when it happened,

00:11:09.626 --> 00:11:12.096
everybody had to pick up the pace.

00:11:12.096 --> 00:11:14.304
All the news media had
to pick up the pace.

00:11:14.304 --> 00:11:16.870
They were bookin' night
flights and flying over here

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:19.326
and flying over there,
somebody had to work over time.

00:11:19.326 --> 00:11:20.996
"Wont' be home for three days."

00:11:20.996 --> 00:11:23.186
Typin' in the middle of the
night, research goin' on.

00:11:23.186 --> 00:11:24.943
Because when somethin' happens,

00:11:24.943 --> 00:11:27.531
everybody got to pick up the pace!

00:11:27.531 --> 00:11:30.405
That's why I can't deal with people

00:11:30.405 --> 00:11:32.983
who cannot pick up the pace.

00:11:32.983 --> 00:11:37.277
Don't be strollin', when
I got to a 9-1-1 on you.

00:11:37.277 --> 00:11:40.193
I need people who can pick up the pace!

00:11:40.193 --> 00:11:42.443
(applause)

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:46.892
Front your neighbor and
say, "Pick up the pace!"

00:11:46.892 --> 00:11:47.725
- [Audience] Pick up the pace!

00:11:47.725 --> 00:11:49.482
- Something's about to happen.

00:11:49.482 --> 00:11:51.667
Pick up the pace,
something's about to happen.

00:11:51.667 --> 00:11:53.836
Pick up the pace,
something's about to happen.

00:11:53.836 --> 00:11:56.026
Pick up the pace,
something's about to happen.

00:11:56.026 --> 00:11:58.242
Pick up the pace, something
is about to happen.

00:11:58.242 --> 00:12:00.344
Pick up the pace,
something's about to happen.

00:12:00.344 --> 00:12:02.972
I came to tell the young
people, pick up the pace,

00:12:02.972 --> 00:12:04.717
pick up the pace, pick up the pace,

00:12:04.717 --> 00:12:07.542
something is about to happen!

00:12:07.542 --> 00:12:10.065
The danger of low expectations.

00:12:10.065 --> 00:12:11.482
- [Audience] Boo!

00:12:13.079 --> 00:12:17.197
- I would rather aim for
the stars and not hit them

00:12:17.197 --> 00:12:19.114
than to not aim at all.

00:12:20.006 --> 00:12:22.511
I would rather go after it and not get it

00:12:22.511 --> 00:12:24.901
than not go after it at all.

00:12:24.901 --> 00:12:29.060
I'd rather try and fail
than not try at all.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:32.248
I don't want to live with the
idea, wonder what would have

00:12:32.248 --> 00:12:35.657
happened, had I done more with my life.

00:12:35.657 --> 00:12:40.062
I'm going to go for it,
come hell or high water.

00:12:40.062 --> 00:12:43.099
I'm goin' after my destiny!

00:12:43.099 --> 00:12:45.239
Touch your neighbor and say, "run!"

00:12:45.239 --> 00:12:46.679
- [Audience] Run!

00:12:46.679 --> 00:12:49.240
- You got to run after your destiny.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:51.974
You can't stroll after your destiny.

00:12:51.974 --> 00:12:54.742
You can't walk after your destiny.

00:12:54.742 --> 00:12:57.575
You got to run! Somebody holla run!

00:12:58.779 --> 00:13:00.196
- [Audience] Run!

00:13:01.404 --> 00:13:03.654
(applause)

00:13:04.923 --> 00:13:06.642
- You got to run.

00:13:06.642 --> 00:13:08.268
You got to run.

00:13:08.268 --> 00:13:09.766
You got to run.

00:13:09.766 --> 00:13:11.309
You can't just wake up in the mornin',

00:13:11.309 --> 00:13:14.029
"Let me see what's gon' happen today.

00:13:14.029 --> 00:13:15.867
I don't know what I'm gon' do.

00:13:15.867 --> 00:13:17.532
I don't know what I'm gon' wear.

00:13:17.532 --> 00:13:18.773
I don't know what I'm gon' cook.

00:13:18.773 --> 00:13:20.168
I don't know where I'm gon' go.

00:13:20.168 --> 00:13:21.651
I just woke up."

00:13:21.651 --> 00:13:23.902
Oh, you should stay in the bed.

00:13:23.902 --> 00:13:28.621
Give today to somebody who's
gon' run after their destiny.

00:13:28.621 --> 00:13:33.211
Give today to somebody who has
a plan, who has a strategy.

00:13:33.211 --> 00:13:36.010
Because success is never an accident.

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:39.011
And if you don't want
it, get out of my way.

00:13:39.011 --> 00:13:42.524
Because there are some people
who want to do something

00:13:42.524 --> 00:13:45.024
with their life, who will run.

00:13:46.018 --> 00:13:47.288
- When I was in the seventh grade,

00:13:47.288 --> 00:13:49.310
my buddy moved away to Oregon.

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:52.917
There was a week where I went
up to visit him in Portland.

00:13:52.917 --> 00:13:55.147
I flew up there by
myself, go to his house,

00:13:55.147 --> 00:13:57.119
and the whole thing was
is, "Hey, he's going to be

00:13:57.119 --> 00:13:59.322
in school on some of these days this week,

00:13:59.322 --> 00:14:01.562
so you can shadow him to school,

00:14:01.562 --> 00:14:03.778
or you can hang out until
he gets out of school."

00:14:03.778 --> 00:14:05.837
I shadow him one day and I was
like, "This is fuckin' weird,

00:14:05.837 --> 00:14:07.268
I'm going to stay at your house and wait."

00:14:07.268 --> 00:14:09.368
But in his room, there were four things

00:14:09.368 --> 00:14:11.510
that were very important.

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:15.663
A Stiff Little Finger's
record, there was a All record,

00:14:15.663 --> 00:14:20.378
the Dinosaur Jr. record, and
there was an electric guitar.

00:14:20.378 --> 00:14:23.145
So, what I did was, I would
play those three albums

00:14:23.145 --> 00:14:26.056
on vinyl, and I would go
over and pick up this guitar

00:14:26.056 --> 00:14:28.026
to keep myself entertained
throughout the day

00:14:28.026 --> 00:14:30.462
for those three or four days
that he would be at school.

00:14:30.462 --> 00:14:32.097
Until he would come back
and we would skate at night

00:14:32.097 --> 00:14:33.608
and do whatever.

00:14:33.608 --> 00:14:35.217
That changed my life.

00:14:35.217 --> 00:14:37.497
You know, changed my life.

00:14:37.497 --> 00:14:39.747
The hearing punk rock music

00:14:41.077 --> 00:14:43.031
and picking up the guitar,

00:14:43.031 --> 00:14:46.410
something clicked where it's almost like,

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:47.941
there's a bunch of gasoline on the ground

00:14:47.941 --> 00:14:50.297
and someone flicks a
cigarette and it just ignites.

00:14:50.297 --> 00:14:51.565
You know, it's just ...

00:14:51.565 --> 00:14:55.246
It was a chemical reaction
that just flipped on a switch

00:14:55.246 --> 00:14:58.408
that nothing could take
that guitar out of my hand

00:14:58.408 --> 00:15:00.118
from that point forward.

00:15:00.118 --> 00:15:04.345
- I think that personal
ambition is worth fighting for.

00:15:04.345 --> 00:15:07.545
It really is something that,
if you don't fight for,

00:15:07.545 --> 00:15:09.510
you're going to regret it
for the rest of your life.

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:11.469
And if you regret it, you're
going to be an unhappy person.

00:15:11.469 --> 00:15:13.405
If you're an unhappy person,
it's going to affect your family.

00:15:13.405 --> 00:15:16.640
So you can see the chain
of command all the way down

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:19.454
that it can be pretty devastating.

00:15:19.454 --> 00:15:22.424
The common asset is we
fight for our family.

00:15:22.424 --> 00:15:27.005
Uh, yeah, but fighting for
family starts with you.

00:15:27.005 --> 00:15:29.090
So, you got to fight for peace of mind.

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:31.402
That's what I think you have to go for.

00:15:31.402 --> 00:15:35.616
You know, what makes you
happy enough in your life

00:15:35.616 --> 00:15:37.991
that you want to make other people happy.

00:15:37.991 --> 00:15:41.056
- High performance is anything but easy.

00:15:41.056 --> 00:15:44.886
And staying on top's even
harder than getting to the top.

00:15:44.886 --> 00:15:46.865
Now, I've been on the
top of my game, arguably,

00:15:46.865 --> 00:15:49.282
for three and a half decades.

00:15:50.439 --> 00:15:53.272
I haven't had to work in 35 years.

00:15:54.146 --> 00:15:58.240
People ask me how do I
get up in the morning?

00:15:58.240 --> 00:15:59.740
I get up fired up.

00:16:01.222 --> 00:16:05.473
I'm fired up, I've been
high on life since 1974.

00:16:05.473 --> 00:16:07.528
That I thought about it and, actually,

00:16:07.528 --> 00:16:11.195
since I got OCS fifty years ago, today.

00:16:11.195 --> 00:16:13.508
Where failure's not an option.

00:16:13.508 --> 00:16:17.341
And I do fail, but when
I do fail, I am so ...

00:16:18.364 --> 00:16:19.857
I can't believe it!

00:16:19.857 --> 00:16:23.088
It must be an error; there must be a typo.

00:16:23.088 --> 00:16:25.401
Because I'm so used to winning.

00:16:25.401 --> 00:16:26.751
